															</div>
				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/jack-grimm" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(6365797); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=6365797&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1605928835" alt="Jack Grimm" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=6365797)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/jack-grimm" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(6365797); return false;" >Jack Grimm</a></span> <span class="odate time_1604433092 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">03 Nov 2020 19:51</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4810641">
									

<p>SCP-001 &quot;When Day Breaks&quot; is told in the form of a story. But there's something that bothers me. If everyone on Earth was &quot;melted&quot; by the sun, and the main character of the story was dragged into the sun, then how were these events discovered and added to the SCP files? In fact, how was &quot;When Day Breaks&quot; even discovered? Did the Foundation witness these events from a different dimension/universe?</p>
<p>What is the range that the sun's anomalous effects take place? Say if someone was in a distant solar system, would they be affected by our sun's anomalous effects or not?</p>
<p>If I recall correctly, SCP-239 is capable of making her thoughts become reality. The file did say that she can only affect her immediate surroundings, but Dr. Clef stated that she could change reality, so maybe she could be able to revert everything to normal so long as she doesn't come into contact with the sun as it nullifies anomalous effects of beings.</p>
<p>Sorry if everything isn't organized. I'm just spewing out ideas here. Please feel free to answer my questions or to add more questions or theories.</p>

							</div>

								
					
