<blockquote>
<p>Did the Foundation witness these events from a different dimension/universe?</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I think you're trying to analyze the format screw too deeply. By its end, Shaggy's Proposal is essentially a tale, not something that's trying to fit into the Foundation's database; if you have to have some justification then just say the sun had some anomalous influence over the contents of the article, I guess, which makes sense given how much each iteration corrupts.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>What is the range that the sun's anomalous effects take place?</p>
</blockquote>
<p>It's not stated, so I guess as far as the light of the sun can travel.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>so maybe she could be able to revert everything to normal so long as she doesn't come into contact with the sun as it nullifies anomalous effects of beings.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Maybe. But she doesn't appear in the article so I guess that doesn't happen within the story's timeframe.</p>

