<blockquote>
<p>then how were these events discovered and added to the SCP files?</p>
</blockquote>
<p>It's pretty clear that not everyone was caught in it at first, some people were inside or in shelter. The character in the story is reading drafts that were written and updated as more and more people were lost to it, all written before he got there.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>What is the range that the sun's anomalous effects take place?</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Don't think it was stated iirc. I mean, the assumption is that most people are on Earth. The O5s wanted to launch space shuttles, but it's unclear if that would've worked.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>so maybe she could be able to revert everything to normal so long as she doesn't come into contact with the sun as it nullifies anomalous effects of beings.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I mean, maybe, but there are a lot of assumptions/things that need to go right for that to work. (She's awake from her coma, she's able to understand everything when asked, the people at her site are unaffected enough to help, etc). Not every SCP gets a happy ending, especially when they were written for the Doomsday Contest.</p>

